    <bpmn:process id="W_W618" name="W618. Customer Churn Prediction &amp; Proactive Retention Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: System churn risk model generates risk score; weekly review trigger
Frequency: Weekly model refresh; daily monitoring; monthly retention review
Volume: ~600,000 loyalty members; ~5,200 trade accounts; ~200 corporate accounts
Owner: CX Analyst
Participants: CX Analyst, Key Account Manager (B2B), Marketing Specialist, CRM Manager
Source: workflow W618 — Customer Churn Prediction &amp; Proactive Retention Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W618_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W618_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W618_Lane2" name="CX Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W618_Lane3" name="Marketing Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W618_Lane4" name="Key Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W618_Lane5" name="Data Scientist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W618_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W618_Start7" name="System churn risk model generates risk score; weekly review trigger">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W618_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W618_Task8" name="Weekly: churn prediction model (ML-based) refreshes risk scores for all active…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly: churn prediction model (ML-based) refreshes risk scores for all active customers using behavioral signals: (a) purchase frequency decline (&gt; 30% drop vs. 90-day average), (b) average basket size decline, (c) last transaction recency (&gt; 60 days for previously monthly shoppers), (d) reduced category breadth, (e) negative feedback (per W608), (f) unresolved complaint (per W41), (g) competitive offer detected (for B2B)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W618_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W618_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W618_Task9" name="System classifies customers into churn risk tiers: High Risk (score &gt; 0.7…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System classifies customers into churn risk tiers: High Risk (score &gt; 0.7, estimated 30-day churn probability), Medium Risk (0.4-0.7), Low Risk (&lt; 0.4); generates weekly churn risk list prioritized by customer lifetime value (CLV) × churn probability
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W618_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W618_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W618_Task10" name="CX Analyst reviews High Risk list weekly; segments by customer type (B2C…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CX Analyst reviews High Risk list weekly; segments by customer type (B2C loyalty, trade, corporate) and root cause; assigns retention actions: (a) B2C loyalty — automated win-back campaign (bonus points offer, personalized discount), (b) Trade account — Key Account Manager personal outreach, (c) Corporate — executive-level engagement
Responsible (R): CX Analyst
Accountable (A): CRM Manager
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W618_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W618_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W618_Task11" name="For B2C loyalty High Risk: Marketing Specialist configures automated retention…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For B2C loyalty High Risk: Marketing Specialist configures automated retention campaign via CDP (per W156): triggered email/SMS with personalized offer based on past purchase categories, 2x loyalty points for next purchase, or exclusive access to new products; 7-day campaign window
Responsible (R): Marketing Specialist
Accountable (A): CRM Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W618_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W618_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W618_Task12" name="For B2B High Risk: Key Account Manager conducts personal outreach within 48…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: For B2B High Risk: Key Account Manager conducts personal outreach within 48 hours; investigates root cause (competitor pricing, service issue, project completion); offers remediation (price review per W163, service improvement, dedicated support); documents outcome in CRM
Responsible (R): Key Account Manager
Accountable (A): Trade Sales Manager
Duration: 30 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W618_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W618_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W618_Task13" name="System tracks retention campaign outcomes: customer responded (Y/N), subsequent…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: System tracks retention campaign outcomes: customer responded (Y/N), subsequent purchase within 30 days, revenue retained; auto-calculates retention rate by intervention type for ROI measurement
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W618_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W618_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W618_Task14" name="Monthly: CX Analyst generates churn analytics report — churn rate by segment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly: CX Analyst generates churn analytics report — churn rate by segment, retention rate by intervention type, revenue at risk, revenue retained, model accuracy (predicted vs. actual churn); presents to CRM Manager and CMO
Responsible (R): CX Analyst
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W618_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W618_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W618_Task15" name="Quarterly: Data Science team recalibrates churn prediction model using actual…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly: Data Science team recalibrates churn prediction model using actual churn outcomes; adjusts feature weights; adds new behavioral signals; validates model accuracy (target AUC &gt; 0.80)
Responsible (R): Data Scientist
Accountable (A): CX Analyst
Duration: 8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W618_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W618_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W618_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W618_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W618_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-280 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Data &amp; CRM (PA-13.3).) | - operational: quarterly model recalibration and human review before high-cost interventions; operational: CLV-weighted prioritization — only intervene for customers where retained CLV exceeds intervention cost; operational: contact frequency limits and opt-out compliance per RA 10173
Owner: CX Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
