    <bpmn:process id="W_W619" name="W619. Customer Account Merge &amp; Deduplication Request Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Duplicate customer detected by system or reported by staff/customer; periodic dedup scan
Frequency: Continuous automated detection; weekly batch processing
Volume: ~200–300 duplicate pairs detected/week across ~600,000 loyalty + ~5,400 B2B accounts
Owner: CRM Data Steward
Participants: CRM Data Steward, Customer Service Counter staff, Key Account Manager (B2B), IT Data Quality Analyst
Source: workflow W619 — Customer Account Merge &amp; Deduplication Request Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W619_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W619_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W619_Lane2" name="CRM Data Steward">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W619_Lane3" name="Key Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W619_Lane4" name="CS Counter Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W619_Lane5" name="Data Quality Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W619_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W619_Start7" name="Duplicate customer detected by system or reported by staff/customer; periodic dedup scan">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W619_Task8" name="System continuously scans for duplicate customer records using matching rules…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System continuously scans for duplicate customer records using matching rules: (a) exact mobile number match, (b) exact email match, (c) name + address fuzzy match (&gt; 90% similarity), (d) same loyalty card registered to different accounts, (e) B2B: same TIN registered to different trade accounts
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W619_Task9" name="System classifies match confidence: Confirmed Duplicate (&gt; 95% match on key…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System classifies match confidence: Confirmed Duplicate (&gt; 95% match on key identifiers), Probable Duplicate (80-95%), Possible Duplicate (60-80%); auto-queues Probable and Possible for human review
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W619_Task10" name="Confirmed Duplicates">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Confirmed Duplicates: system auto-merges with survivorship rules — (a) keep account with earlier creation date as primary, (b) merge transaction history, (c) consolidate loyalty points balances, (d) prefer verified contact info, (e) retain all addresses; auto-merge generates audit trail for compliance (per W253)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): CRM Data Steward
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W619_Task11" name="Probable Duplicates">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Probable Duplicates: CRM Data Steward reviews each pair on the dedup workbench — the Oracle Customer Data Librarian steward console (fit-gap D20), displaying both records side-by-side with highlighted differences; Steward confirms merge, rejects as non-duplicate, or requests more information
Responsible (R): CRM Data Steward
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/pair</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W619_Task12" name="Possible Duplicates">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Possible Duplicates: system flags for periodic batch review; CRM Data Steward reviews weekly batch of low-confidence matches; marks as duplicate or not-duplicate to improve matching algorithm
Responsible (R): CRM Data Steward
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3 min/pair</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W619_Task13" name="B2B dedup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: B2B dedup: for trade/corporate accounts, dedup is more sensitive (tax implications of merged accounts); Key Account Manager confirms B2B merges; Finance Analyst validates that open AR/AP, credit limits, and tax registrations are correctly consolidated
Responsible (R): Key Account Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Analyst
Duration: 15 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W619_Task14" name="Customer-initiated merge">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Customer-initiated merge: customer reports duplicate account at Customer Service Counter or via app; staff creates merge request with customer-verified information; CRM Data Steward processes within 2 business days
Responsible (R): CS Counter Staff
Accountable (A): CRM Data Steward
Duration: 10 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W619_Task15" name="Weekly: CRM Data Steward generates dedup metrics — new duplicates detected…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Weekly: CRM Data Steward generates dedup metrics — new duplicates detected, auto-merged, manually reviewed, merge rejection rate, and total active duplicate rate; reports to CRM Manager and Data Quality Analyst
Responsible (R): CRM Data Steward
Accountable (A): CRM Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W619_Task16" name="Monthly: IT Data Quality Analyst reviews matching algorithm performance — false…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Monthly: IT Data Quality Analyst reviews matching algorithm performance — false positive rate, false negative rate, and new duplicate creation rate; adjusts matching thresholds and adds new matching rules as needed
Responsible (R): Data Quality Analyst
Accountable (A): CRM Data Steward
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W619_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W619_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W619_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W619_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-280 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Data &amp; CRM (PA-13.3).) | - operational: human review for Probable matches and survivorship rule validation; operational: pre-merge points balance confirmation and 30-day merge reversal capability; operational: mandatory Finance Analyst review for B2B merges in Step 6
Owner: CRM Data Steward</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W619_Assoc19" sourceRef="W619_Annotation18" targetRef="W619_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
