    <bpmn:process id="W_W782" name="W782. Customer B2B Order-to-Cash Cycle Monitoring &amp; Proactive Communication" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: B2B customer order placement; or weekly proactive monitoring cycle
Frequency: Continuous order monitoring; weekly proactive communication cycle
Volume: ~5,200 trade accounts + ~200 corporate accounts; ~3,500 AR invoices/month
Owner: Key Account Manager
Participants: Key Account Manager, Sales Coordinator, AR Accountant, Logistics Coordinator, Customer
Source: workflow W782 — Customer B2B Order-to-Cash Cycle Monitoring &amp; Proactive Communication</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W782_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W782_Lane1" name="KAM">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W782_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W782_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W782_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W782_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W782_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W782_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W782_Lane2" name="Sales Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W782_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W782_Lane3" name="AR Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W782_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W782_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W782_Start5" name="B2B customer order placement; or weekly proactive monitoring cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W782_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W782_Task6" name="Weekly order pipeline review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly order pipeline review: Key Account Manager reviews all active B2B orders: (a) orders pending fulfillment ( &gt; SLA target: 3 business days for DC stock, 10 days for procurement), (b) orders with partial delivery — outstanding items, (c) delivered but not invoiced, (d) invoiced but not yet due, (e) overdue invoices per W108 aging
Responsible (R): KAM
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W782_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W782_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W782_Task7" name="Stalled order intervention">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Stalled order intervention: For orders stalled at any stage: (a) fulfillment delay — contact DC per W584 to expedite or identify stockout, (b) delivery delay — contact Logistics per W268 for carrier status, (c) invoicing delay — coordinate with AR per W8 to ensure timely invoice generation, (d) proactively communicate status to customer per W708 with revised timeline
Responsible (R): KAM
Accountable (A): Sales Manager
Duration: 30 min/stalled order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W782_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W782_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W782_Task8" name="Pre-delivery customer confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pre-delivery customer confirmation: Before dispatch of large B2B orders (&gt; PHP 100,000): (a) Sales Coordinator calls customer to confirm delivery readiness (site access, unloading crew, payment terms), (b) confirm delivery address and special instructions, (c) verify credit limit has available headroom per W572, (d) resolve any issues before truck dispatch
Responsible (R): Sales Coordinator
Accountable (A): KAM
Duration: 15 min/order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W782_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W782_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W782_Task9" name="Delivery confirmation and invoice trigger">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Delivery confirmation and invoice trigger: Post-delivery: (a) system generates delivery confirmation with POD per W592, (b) AR Accountant generates sales invoice per W8 with correct payment terms (Net 30/60/90 per W295), (c) system sends invoice to customer via W708 (email with PDF attachment), (d) KAM follows up within 24 hours to confirm invoice receipt
Responsible (R): AR Accountant / System
Accountable (A): KAM
Duration: Automated + 10 min follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W782_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W782_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W782_Task10" name="Proactive payment follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Proactive payment follow-up: Before invoice due date: (a) T-7 days: friendly reminder per W708 (&quot;Your invoice #[X] for PHP [Y] is due on [Date]. Please arrange payment.&quot;), (b) T-3 days: phone call or SMS to confirm payment scheduling, (c) Due date: payment received check; if not — escalate per W108 collection process
Responsible (R): KAM / AR Accountant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5-10 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W782_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W782_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W782_Task11" name="Monthly order-to-cash metrics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly order-to-cash metrics: KAM reports: (a) average order-to-delivery time (target: &lt; 5 business days), (b) delivery-to-invoice time (target: &lt; 2 business days), (c) average DSO per W108 (target: ≤ 45 days), (d) order-to-cash cycle time (target: &lt; 50 days), (e) stalled order rate, (f) customer satisfaction with B2B service per W617 QBR
Responsible (R): KAM
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W782_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W782_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W782_Task12" name="Quarterly top account deep dive">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly top account deep dive: For top 50 B2B accounts: (a) order-to-cash cycle analysis per account, (b) recurring bottlenecks identification, (c) process improvement recommendations, (d) customer feedback integration per W617 QBR
Responsible (R): KAM
Accountable (A): Sales Manager
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W782_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W782_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W782_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W782_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W782_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-280 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Data &amp; CRM (PA-13.3).) | - operational: Key Account Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Key Account Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W782_Assoc15" sourceRef="W782_Annotation14" targetRef="W782_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
